{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Another occurrence, plus what looks like the exact root cause and a one-line fix already proven in a sibling file.\n\n**Occurrence.** Hit on change 1715 (ticket statuesque-glycemic-iguana, a pure `src/rebar/_store/` module split that touches no reconciler and no test): CI `Verified -1`, macOS shard only, ubuntu shards green, single failing test `test_pass_summary_reports_the_decline_count`. Also reproduced LOCALLY on that tree under the same invocation (`-n 3 --dist worksteal`): 1 failed, 12699 passed. That makes at least three independent changes now red-lit by it (this one, `unheedful-custodial-bluebottle`, and the original report).\n\n**Mechanism, confirmed from the captured records.** The assertion failure prints the caplog contents, and they contain the PER-LINK decline message but not the pass SUMMARY. Those two differ only in level:\n- per-link decline -> `logger.warning` (`apply_inbound_records`, the \"declining the inbound removal of ...\" record)\n- pass summary -> `logger.info` (the \"declined %d inbound link removal(s)\" record the assertion greps for)\n\nSo the record is being dropped AT THE ORIGINATING LOGGER, not at the handler — the signature of a leaked `setLevel(WARNING)` above INFO on `rebar_reconciler.apply_inbound_records`. Under xdist that leak only matters when the poisoning test happens to land on the same worker ahead of this one, which is exactly why it is intermittent and shard-dependent.\n\n**The fix is already in the repo, in the sibling file.** `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_link_removal_2b16.py` hit this before (bug 9ac2) and defends against it:\n\n    # Pin the level ON THE ORIGINATING LOGGER: it lives outside the `rebar` hierarchy\n    # that tests/conftest.py's propagation guard restores, so a leaked\n    # setLevel(WARNING) from an earlier full-suite test would otherwise drop this\n    # INFO record at the source and make the assertion below unreachable (bug 9ac2).\n    with caplog.at_level(\"INFO\", logger=apply_records.logger.name):\n\n`test_pass_summary_reports_the_decline_count` in `test_inbound_removal_confirmation_a4bd.py` still uses the bare form, `with caplog.at_level(logging.INFO):`, which raises only the ROOT level and leaves a leaked level on the originating logger in place. Changing it to the `logger=apply_records.logger.name` form should close this deterministically, matching the precedent 9ac2 already set.\n\nWorth checking the rest of the a4bd file for the same bare form while fixing — and note `tests/unit/test_caplog_coverage_integrity.py` deliberately exercises `logging.getLogger(\"rebar\").setLevel(logging.WARNING)` as a \"leaks today\" scenario, so a poisoner of this shape demonstrably exists in the suite.\n\nNot fixing it here — this is a different ticket and I hold statuesque-glycemic-iguana, not this one. Filing the analysis so whoever claims this can go straight to the change."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786612359078290001,"uuid":"eb563af7-fc16-40aa-a79e-b49b9cf21583"}